<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alaric II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 507</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alaric II was king of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/visigoths">Visigoths</a> from 484 to 507, ruling much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaul">Gaul</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Hispania</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toulouse">Toulouse</a>. In 486 he handed over the fugitive Roman ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syagrius">Syagrius</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clovis-i">Clovis</a>, and in 506 he issued the Breviary of Alaric, a digest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-law">Roman law</a> for his Roman subjects. He was killed by Clovis at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-vouille">Battle of Vouillé</a> in 507.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alaric-ii.jpg" alt="Alaric II" width="320" height="487" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anneau_sigillaire_Alaric_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
